 198: /// a renderer is free to ignore the ones it does not need.
 199: ///
 200: /// Row-level chrome such as the [BlockDragHandleSpec] surface is deliberately
 201: /// editor-owned and sits outside renderer output. Renderers paint block content
 202: /// only, which keeps default drag handles available to custom renderers and
 203: /// prevents nested table-cell text or inline/object controls from becoming
 204: /// sortable rows.
